# Catalan keeps its vowels apart where Castilian runs them together.
#
# syneresis is the pass that makes two vowels into one syllable, and Castilian
# wants it: duana is [dwana] there. Catalan says the two, and the words where
# it does not are the ones a dictionary knows rather than a rule. With
# Castilian's pass in, duana came out [d w a n @], suau [s w a w] and serie
# [s E r y @], each a syllable short, and the letter rules had laid both
# vowels down correctly before it ran.
#
# So this is the same rule with the merging taken out: it takes what it is
# given, answers where the run ends unchanged, and lays nothing down. The
# frame and the two pointers are IBM's, because the caller passes them and
# reads the second one back.
rule syneresis takes 3 from st_phnol.obj
  local left bytes 8
  local right bytes 8
  call ZZget_parm_ptr2 addr left arg 1 addr right arg 2
  call ZZfence_null
  call succeed
  put cell right value into arg 2 at 4
  answer 0
end
